# Row 19's imported-project route, re-rendered with the CPU-property guard in
#
# What was unmeasured: `ImportProject(file)` then `LoadProject(<name>)` then a
# frame. 2026-11-26 got as far as opening the imported project with the effect on
# the item, and the frame was the source pixel for pixel because the host refused
# the plug-in (`describe failed ... error code 4`, `plugin is not available`).
# That refusal was one write in `describe()`, `kOfxImageEffectPropCPURenderSupported`,
# guarded since commit be06bc4. This is the same route on a bundle built after it.

## 1. the first attempt ran a bundle older than the guard, and reproduced the old failure

Bundle: `.validation/build-provider-only`, provider-only (ONNX Runtime 1.20.1, no
CUDA runtime of its own), `OnnxInference.ofx` 193,024 bytes, 2026-11-26 22:25.

  test/run-tests.bat is not involved here; the host is:
  python tests/resolve/poc.py --bundle … --import-project .validation/drp/row19-recheck.drp \
      --reference .validation/resolve-source.png --expect 1920x1080

  import    pass   ImportProject -> True, LoadProject('row19-recheck') -> project
  render    pass   Complete, 100%, row19_00108000.png, 1920x1080
  image             mae 0.0, max_pixel 0, compared_bytes 8294400 - identical to the source
  ONNX_PROVIDER_LOG absent: no instance was ever created

Host log, that session (19:55):

  Plugin [com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference] is not available!!!!        many
  Create context [OfxImageEffectContextFilter_ae417e8d-…] failed for plugin […]
                                                                            dozens

So the frame was the source because the host skipped the effect, exactly as on
2026-11-26: the bundle predates the guard, and the run proves the route and
nothing about the plug-in.

## 2. rebuilt from the tree that has the guard

  cmake --build .validation/build-provider-only --config Release --parallel   -> 0
  OnnxInference.ofx 209,408 bytes, 2026-11-27 19:56

## 3. what ImportProject answers when the name is already in the library

`ImportProject` does not say "the file is bad" when it answers False. From a host
that already holds `row19-import` in its current folder:

  LoadProject('row19-import') before any import          -> True
  ImportProject('…/row19-import.drp')                    -> False
  GetProjectListInCurrentFolder() after it               -> … 'row19', 'row19-import' …
  LoadProject('row19-import') after it                   -> project
  project.GetName()                                      -> 'row19-import'
  project.GetCurrentTimeline().GetName()                 -> 'row19'
  timeline items on video 1                              -> 1
  item.GetEffects('ofx')                                 -> 1
  item.GetName()                                         -> 'resolve-source.png'

False is "skipped, a project of that name exists", so a re-import of the same
file name is not a re-import. `resolve_api.import_project` returns the pair
`(project, imported)` for that reason and `poc.py` reports which one happened.

## 4. the start: -nogui was not answering, the UI was

Four `-nogui` launches in a row on 2026-11-27: two wrote

  Failed to connect to script server
  801.703 [ 4076] Incoming connection
  801.703 [ 4076] HostApp create
  801.703 [ 4076] RemoteApp::Connect (00000000000002AC) - ioctlsocket(block) err 1
  801.812 [ 4076] HostApp destroy

and two reached `TimeoutError: no Resolve after 300s`. The same executable with
its UI (`poc.py --gui`, launched 20:31:12) connected in 23 s. `-nogui` had
answered 40 minutes earlier on the same build, so this is the start the notes
already call unreliable, not a property of the bundle.

## 5. the route, end to end, on the guarded bundle

  python tests/resolve/poc.py \
      --bundle .validation/build-provider-only/bundle/OnnxInference.ofx.bundle \
      --import-project .validation/drp/row19-final.drp \
      --reference .validation/resolve-source.png --expect 1920x1080 \
      --out .validation/frames-row19-final --gui

  validate  pass     1 .ofx, decoders ['ffmpeg']
  install   pass     C:\Program Files\Common Files\OFX\Plugins\OnnxInference.ofx.bundle
  launch    pass     pid 16312
  connect   pass     DaVinci Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5
  gpu       pass     Compute API set to automatic, defaulting to CUDA; Selected compute API: CUDA
  load      pass     row19-final.drp project format
  render    pass     poc00108000.png
  check     fail     mae 94.873 > 0.0; max pixel error 255 > 0.0
  quit      pass     API quit, then the recorded PID

  report: tests/resolve/reports/poc-2026-11-27T19-31-12+00-00.json
  image: 1920x1080, 4 channels, decoder ffmpeg, mae 94.872843, max_pixel 255

`check` fails because `--reference` demands identity and this plug-in is not an
identity: the model's output differs from the source by mae 94.873, which is the
figure the CPU-path run of the same bundle produced against the same source
earlier that day (94.87, `resolve-onnx-host-report.json`). A frame that differs
from the source by the model's own error is what a render looks like; an
identical frame is what a skipped effect looks like.

The plug-in's own label, read from `$ONNX_PROVIDER_LOG`:

  CUDA (device 0, 1 thread, bundled CUDA, tf32 off, arena kSameAsRequested, all
  nodes on CUDA) | C:\Program Files\Common Files\OFX\Plugins\OnnxInference.ofx.bundle\Contents\Win64/../Resources/model.onnx

Two things there are not incidental: the session is on CUDA with every node on
it, and the model came from `Contents/Resources/model.onnx` - the second branch,
not `ONNX_MODEL_PATH` - because this run set no variable. The imported project
carried the effect; the bundle carried the model.

Host log, same session:

  OFX: loading com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference             20:14:49 (earlier run), 20:31
  Create context … onnxinference failed                         0 occurrences

`timeline.GetSetting("timelineFrameWidth")` and `…Height` both answer `''` on a
project opened this way, so the render keeps the project's format; the frame came
out 1920x1080, the timeline's size.

## 6. what this closes, and what it does not

Closes: the imported-project half of row 19. With the guard in, a `.drp` exported
by this host is imported, opened by its base name, and renders the plug-in's
output - no parameter setter, no GUI click, no model path in the project.

Does not close, and is not claimed here:

  - the `-nogui` start: no attempt reached a scriptable host on this machine today,
    so the route is measured on a UI start only;
  - a second GPU or a machine without the CUDA 12 runtime the provider needs;
  - a `.drp` that carries a *non-default* parameter: the exported project carries
    the effect with its defaults, and there is still no setter;
  - repeatability of the import: the second import of the same file name is
    skipped, so a fresh measurement needs a fresh file name.
